  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 104 PM Tuesday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Seasonable and dry fall weather through much of the \nperiod. Below normal highs expected Friday through Sunday behind \nreinforcing cool high pressure.\n\nA very quiet stretch of weather will persist well into at least the \nearly part of next week. Cool surface high pressure will remain \nanchored across the northeast and Mid-Atlantic states through much \nof the week and weekend. \n\nA reinforcing cool high pressure system will build down Friday and \npersist into early next week. High temperatures will largely hover \nnear normal in the upper 60s to lower 70s each afternoon. The one \nexception will be this late week and weekend, when highs in the low \nto mid 60s are favored under that cool high pressure. We may even \nhave some patchy frost Saturday and Sunday mornings as lows range \nfrom the upper 30s to middle 40s, with middle 30s in the typical \ncooler spots.\n\nDue to the pattern, there is virtually no threat of rain. Ensemble \ndata suggest perhaps a chance by the middle of next week, but that \nchance at this point is fairly low.",
